Subject: [PATCH] Local pipeline engine: faster-whisper + Nemotron-3 speaker labels, export folder

Adds a 'local-pipeline' transcription engine (faster-whisper large-v3-turbo + NeMo-Speech.cpp
Nemotron-3 diarization, run by a built-in Python script at below-normal priority, Hugging Face
offline), makes it the default for a vault with no transcription setting, adds Settings fields
for its paths (desktop app only) and an export folder written by temp-folder rename.
See docs/local-pipeline.md.
---
diff --git a/docs/local-pipeline.md b/docs/local-pipeline.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cb24b42
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/local-pipeline.md
@@ -0,0 +1,111 @@
+# Local pipeline: faster-whisper + Nemotron-3 speaker labels
+
+The **Local pipeline** engine transcribes on this computer with faster-whisper `large-v3-turbo` and labels
+speakers with NVIDIA's Nemotron-3 diarization model through the NeMo-Speech.cpp command-line tool. It is the
+default engine when a vault has no transcription setting saved. Every option stays selectable in
+**Settings → AI providers**: you can pick another engine, model, language or profile, or turn speaker labels off.
+
+Nothing is sent anywhere. The engine counts as local, so **Local only** mode allows it. Hugging Face is forced
+offline while it runs (`HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`), so a model that is not already in the local cache fails with a clear
+message instead of downloading.
+
+## What it runs
+
+The Python script is built into the OpenPlod service (`src/transcription/local-pipeline.py`). On first use it is
+written to the work folder. Each recording gets its own work folder. The script runs at Windows **below normal**
+CPU priority, and ffmpeg and nemo-speech inherit it.
+
+1. **Decode:** `ffmpeg -v error -y -i <audio> -ac 1 -ar 16000 -c:a pcm_s16le audio16k.wav`. The input is the
+   recording's `decoded-original.ogg` when it has one, otherwise its `.m4a`.
+2. **Speech to text:** `WhisperModel(<model>, device="cpu", compute_type="int8", cpu_threads=<all cores>)`, then
+   `transcribe(samples, language, vad_filter=True, word_timestamps=True, beam_size=5, initial_prompt=<prompt>)`.
+   The samples are float32, read with `soundfile`, because faster-whisper 1.2.1's own decoder breaks on PyAV 19.
+   The initial prompt is the **Context prompt**, then the **Vocabulary hints** as a comma-separated list. Profiles
+   add their own prompt and vocabulary. Writes `asr.json`.
+3. **Speaker labels:** `nemo-speech diarize audio16k.wav --device auto --preset v3-offline --format rttm
+   --recording-id <YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM_meeting> --output diar.rttm --force`. The builds are tried in order (see
+   below), and if one fails the next is tried. Writes `diar.rttm` and `diar.json`, whose `meta.engine` is
+   `nemotron-3-diarization/v3-offline`.
+4. **Merge:** each Whisper segment gets one speaker: the one whose turns overlap it most, else the turn covering
+   its midpoint, else the nearest turn. Never word by word. Consecutive segments with the same speaker are
+   joined when the gap is under 2.0 s. Speakers are named `Speaker A`, `Speaker B`, … in order of first
+   appearance. Writes `transcript.json` and `transcript.md`.
+
+`timing.txt` records `start`, `asr wall_sec`, `diarize wall_sec`, `merge wall_sec` and `end`, or `FAILED <step>`.
+The job list in **Settings → AI providers → Processing jobs** shows the step (1, 2 or 3 of 3) and the percent of
+audio done.
+
+A run is stopped after 3× the audio length plus 15 minutes. **Cancel** stops the script and everything it started.
+
+## Install (once per computer, Windows)
+
+1. **Python with faster-whisper.** The default location is `%LOCALAPPDATA%\plaud-asr\.venv`:
+   ```powershell
+   py -3.12 -m venv "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\plaud-asr\.venv"
+   & "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\plaud-asr\.venv\Scripts\python.exe" -m pip install faster-whisper==1.2.1 soundfile
+   ```
+   Then download the model once, while online, so it is in the Hugging Face cache:
+   ```powershell
+   & "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\plaud-asr\.venv\Scripts\python.exe" -c "from faster_whisper import WhisperModel; WhisperModel('large-v3-turbo', device='cpu', compute_type='int8')"
+   ```
+2. **NeMo-Speech.cpp 0.3.0.** Download `nemo-speech-0.3.0-windows-x86_64-vulkan.zip` (GPU) and
+   `nemo-speech-0.3.0-windows-x86_64-cpu.zip` from
+   <https://github.com/NVIDIA/NeMo-Speech.cpp/releases/tag/v0.3.0>. Check each against that release's
+   `SHA256SUMS`:
+   - cpu: `4ed9740e361e4653f56c3dce7d1e81883a1c8b831c1bd7d01567fff1130b5b05`
+   - vulkan: `72b3b8b41bfe2be0320eff4e9d310594e4f99deefcde4a157799a039656963ce`
+
+   Unzip them to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\nemo-speech\0.3.0-vulkan\` and `%LOCALAPPDATA%\nemo-speech\0.3.0-cpu\`. Then
+   fetch the model once with either build (the tool checks its size and SHA-256 itself):
+   `nemo-speech.exe pull nemotron-3-diarization`.
+3. **ffmpeg.** OpenPlod's Windows installer bundles ffmpeg and puts it first on the service's PATH, so nothing
+   else is needed.
+
+## Settings (Settings → AI providers → Local pipeline)
+
+Leave a field empty to use its default. Each field shows the value it resolves to. Only the desktop app on this
+computer can change these fields: a paired phone or an `OPENPLOD_API_TOKEN` script gets `403`.
+
+| Field | Empty means (in this order) |
+| --- | --- |
+| Pipeline Python | env `PIPELINE_PYTHON`, then `%LOCALAPPDATA%\plaud-asr\.venv\Scripts\python.exe` |
+| nemo-speech.exe | env `NEMO_SPEECH_EXE`, then `%LOCALAPPDATA%\nemo-speech\*vulkan*\…\bin\nemo-speech.exe` (newest first), then `*cpu*` |
+| Work folder | env `PIPELINE_WORK_DIR`, then `%LOCALAPPDATA%\OpenPlodPipeline` |
+| Export (checkbox) | on |
+| Export folder | env `OPENPLOD_EXPORT_DIR`, then `%LOCALAPPDATA%\OpenPlodExport` |
+
+The engine is available when the Python and at least one nemo-speech build are found. Otherwise the error says
+which one is missing.
+
+## Export folder
+
+After each successful local-pipeline transcript with speaker labels, OpenPlod writes one folder per recording:
+
+```
+<export folder>\YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM_meeting\
+    audio.ogg  asr.json  diar.json  diar.rttm  transcript.json  transcript.md  timing.txt
+    openplod.json   {"recording_id", "source_recording_id", "recorded_at", "duration_seconds", "app_version"}
+```
+
+- The name is the local clock time the recording **started**. For a recording read from the recorder over
+  Bluetooth, that comes from its session id (the start time in Unix seconds). OpenPlod's `recorded_at` field
+  holds the import time for those, so it is only used as a fallback.
+- The files are copied into a hidden `.tmp-…` folder inside the export folder and renamed into place at the
+  end. A folder carrying the final name is always complete.
+- An existing folder is never overwritten: the next one is `…_meeting_2`, then `_3`, and so on.
+- With speaker labels off, nothing is exported, because `diar.json` would be missing.
+- A failed export is logged and never fails the transcript.
+
+## Local API
+
+- **Address:** `http://127.0.0.1:3487` (the desktop app's service. The port is fixed in `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`;
+  a source-run server reads `PORT`).
+- **Authentication:** header `X-OpenPlod-Token`. Use the desktop pairing token (the `pairing-token` file in the
+  vault folder; full access over loopback) or a separate `OPENPLOD_API_TOKEN`. See `docs/api.md`,
+  Authentication and Exposure.
+- **List recordings:** `GET /api/recordings?limit=100` (rows include `hasTranscript`).
+- **Get a recording's transcript:** `GET /api/recordings/:id` (current transcript with segments and speakers) or
+  `GET /api/recordings/:id/transcript/versions` (every version with provenance).
+- **Start a transcription:** `POST /api/v1/jobs` with
+  `{"type": "process-recording", "recordingId": "<id>", "confirm": true}`. Watch it with `GET /api/v1/jobs/:id`.
+  The local pipeline needs no cloud consent or cost confirmation.
